Translation patch: construction of `io::Error` in the binlog code

Change: In `binlog/value.rs` and `binlog/events/gtid_event.rs`, `io::Error::new(kind, "..")` / `io::Error::other("..")` become `misc::io_error_msg(kind, "..")` (with `ErrorKind::Other` for `other`), and `.map_err(|e| io::Error::new(kind, e))?` becomes a `match` returning `misc::io_error_from(kind, e)`. In `Event::read_event` the error `io::Error::other(format!("bytes remaining on stream while reading {}", type_name::<T>()))` moves into the new opaque helper `binlog::trusted::bytes_remaining_error::<T>()`.
Why: `io::Error::new` goes through `Box<dyn Error>` (Aeneas: "Dynamic trait types are not supported yet"), and `format!`/`type_name` are not modelled; same as patch 02. Closures: see patch 09.
Behaviour: Identical: `io::Error::other(x)` is `io::Error::new(ErrorKind::Other, x)`; the helpers are the inlined calls; the `match` is the definition of `map_err` followed by `?` (`From<io::Error> for io::Error` is the identity).

